<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Demosthenes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">384–<a href="/years/322-bce">322 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Demosthenes was an Athenian statesman and the greatest orator of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. In speeches such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olynthiacs">Olynthiacs</a> and Philippics he urged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> to resist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II of Macedon</a>, and he helped build the alliance defeated at Chaeronea in 338 BCE. After a failed revolt against Macedonian rule in 322 BCE he took poison to avoid capture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/demosthenes.jpg" alt="Demosthenes" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Polyeuctus · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Demosthenes_Polyeuctos_Louvre_Ma237_n01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
